<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Jan 10.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Jan 10.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 01/10/97  01/03/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    142.12    154.11    61.11	66.27     43.50</p>
<p>West	    121.06    133.60    46.72	51.56     56.70</p>
<p>Total Canada  263.17    287.72    53.53	58.52     50.60</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 01/10/97: 232.55 bcf, 01/03/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 01/10/97: 259.11 bcf, 01/03/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
